{"id": "federal-claims-for-state-only-coverage", "title": "California billed Washington for health coverage only the State may fund", "seconds": 130.2, "voice": "elevenlabs:9PVP7ENhDskL0KYHAKtD", "narrator": "Jerry B.", "tempo": 1.114, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "695a751575e2ec62", "words": 418, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[4]"], "text": "California gives full Medi-Cal to residents without a satisfactory immigration status.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.27, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "Washington", "sub": "emergency and pregnancy care"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "State of California", "sub": "all the rest"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Full Medi-Cal", "sub": "no satisfactory immigration status"}], "kicker": "Who pays for what"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.59, 0.82, 1.06, 1.51, 1.64, 2.04, 2.34, 2.42, 3.1, 3.59]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[4]"], "text": "State law says State money pays for it.", "t0": 4.39, "t1": 6.07, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "Washington", "sub": "emergency and pregnancy care"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "State of California", "sub": "all the rest"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Full Medi-Cal", "sub": "no satisfactory immigration status"}], "kicker": "Who pays for what"}, "emph": ["State money"], "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.52, 0.71, 0.99, 1.2, 1.42, 1.6]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]", "links[0]"], "text": "Washington pays only for their emergency and pregnancy care.", "t0": 6.19, "t1": 8.7, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "Washington", "sub": "emergency and pregnancy care"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "State of California", "sub": "all the rest"}, {"art": "housing", "name": "Full Medi-Cal", "sub": "no satisfactory immigration status"}], "kicker": "Who pays for what"}, "emph": ["only"], "wt": [0.0, 0.45, 0.71, 0.91, 1.03, 1.2, 1.68, 1.79, 2.23]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "span", "ref": ["story[2]", "timeline[0]"], "text": "So the federal inspector general checked nine months of the State’s claims.", "t0": 8.82, "t1": 11.97, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2018-10-01", "to": "2019-06-30", "days": null, "fromLab": "audit begins", "toLab": "audit ends", "kicker": "HHS Office of Inspector General"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.3, 0.61, 1.12, 1.43, 1.72, 1.99, 2.25, 2.32, 2.41, 2.7]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "span", "ref": ["story[2]", "timeline[0]"], "text": "How much federal money went to State-only care?", "t0": 12.09, "t1": 14.7, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2018-10-01", "to": "2019-06-30", "days": null, "fromLab": "audit begins", "toLab": "audit ends", "kicker": "HHS Office of Inspector General"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.45, 0.78, 1.02, 1.2, 1.31, 1.82]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[1]", "amount"], "text": "52,652,689 dollars.", "t0": 14.7, "t1": 16.76, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$52,652,689", "label": "federal Medicaid money improperly claimed", "sub": "October 2018 to June 2019, out of $372.9 million examined"}, "emph": ["52,652,689"], "wt": [0.04, 0.37, 0.87, 1.13, 1.41, 1.71]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[1]", "sources"], "text": "That’s an official finding, from the federal inspector general, in 2024.", "t0": 17.28, "t1": 21.07, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "An official finding", "sub": "U.S. Department of Health and Human Services, Office of Inspector General, 2024"}, "emph": ["official finding"], "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.34, 0.72, 1.27, 1.46, 1.55, 1.85, 2.3, 2.76, 2.93, 3.22]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[0]"], "text": "In September 2025, federal guidance cited that audit as its example of improper claiming.", "t0": 21.19, "t1": 26.08, "shot": "b4g", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "The federal agency’s guidance of September 2025 cites the 2024 audit of California as its example of improper claiming.", "kicker": "Federal guidance, September 2025"}, "emph": ["example"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.61, 0.86, 1.75, 2.09, 2.45, 2.78, 2.94, 3.21, 3.35, 3.52, 4.0, 4.1, 4.51]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[2]", "links[4]"], "text": "How did it happen? The State pays health plans a flat monthly amount per member.", "t0": 26.3, "t1": 29.98, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "State health department", "sub": "pays each plan"}, {"art": "money", "name": "A flat monthly amount", "sub": "per member"}, {"art": "question", "name": "The split", "sub": "federal part, State part"}], "kicker": "How the bill is split"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.33, 0.45, 1.13, 1.27, 1.55, 1.8, 2.01, 2.31, 2.39, 2.65, 2.95, 3.23, 3.38]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[2]", "links[4]"], "text": "Then it splits that into a federal part and a State part.", "t0": 30.1, "t1": 32.68, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "cityhall", "name": "State health department", "sub": "pays each plan"}, {"art": "money", "name": "A flat monthly amount", "sub": "per member"}, {"art": "question", "name": "The split", "sub": "federal part, State part"}], "kicker": "How the bill is split"}, "emph": ["splits"], "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.27, 0.62, 0.79, 1.0, 1.07, 1.39, 1.69, 1.94, 2.01, 2.27]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "story[2]"], "text": "To split it, it used a percentage worked out in the early 2000s.", "t0": 32.8, "t1": 35.86, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "A formula from the early 2000s", "kicker": "Never updated", "sub": "the share used to split the payments"}, "emph": ["early 2000s"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.43, 0.76, 0.89, 1.08, 1.15, 1.63, 1.88, 2.02, 2.1, 2.2, 2.43]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "So an outdated formula moved State costs onto federal taxpayers.", "t0": 35.98, "t1": 39.0, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "An outdated percentage moved State costs onto federal taxpayers."}, "emph": ["federal taxpayers"], "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.28, 0.69, 1.12, 1.36, 1.64, 1.95, 2.14, 2.43]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "story[3]"], "text": "The federal Medicaid agency says the State over-claimed, by its own admission, from at least 2020.", "t0": 39.22, "t1": 44.22, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services", "kicker": "Not just nine months", "sub": "letter of 18 March 2025"}, "emph": ["own admission"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.43, 0.84, 1.27, 1.5, 1.62, 1.9, 2.62, 2.81, 2.94, 3.07, 3.78, 3.99, 4.11, 4.35, 4.66]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[5]", "timeline[7]"], "text": "The State says it found and disclosed the errors itself, in 2020.", "t0": 44.34, "t1": 47.63, "shot": "b8r", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "The State says it found and disclosed the State-only claiming errors itself in 2020.", "kicker": "The State’s reply, 17 February 2026"}, "emph": ["itself"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.39, 0.59, 0.7, 0.96, 1.06, 1.49, 1.62, 1.89, 2.5, 2.66, 2.95]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[2]"], "text": "The agency says it has collected more than 500 million dollars.", "t0": 47.75, "t1": 51.08, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$500 million", "label": "collected, says the federal agency", "sub": "plus $34.1 million found in a separate review, since returned"}, "emph": ["500 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.57, 0.88, 0.98, 1.09, 1.56, 1.74, 1.93, 2.26, 2.59, 2.91]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["oneLine", "timeline[6]"], "text": "In January 2026 the agency told the Governor it was recouping over 1.60 billion dollars from California.", "t0": 51.6, "t1": 57.78, "shot": "b9j", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$1.60 billion", "label": "being recouped from California", "sub": "more than 88% of what the agency is recouping over State-only coverage"}, "emph": ["1.60 billion"], "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.63, 0.88, 1.69, 1.85, 2.21, 2.41, 2.53, 2.85, 2.93, 3.06, 3.5, 3.76, 3.99, 4.3, 4.56, 4.87, 5.21, 5.49, 5.62]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[3]"], "text": "State Medi-Cal spending rose 1.4 billion dollars in 2025–26.", "t0": 58.3, "t1": 62.78, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["State General Fund Medi-Cal spending, 2025–26", "$1.4 billion higher"], "b": ["why", "much of it repayments"], "arrows": false}, "emph": ["1.4 billion"], "wt": [0.0, 0.33, 0.79, 1.16, 1.43, 1.66, 1.93, 2.17, 2.49, 2.84, 2.94, 3.21, 3.78, 3.85]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["established[3]"], "text": "Much of it, the Legislative Analyst says, was repayments.", "t0": 62.9, "t1": 65.85, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["State General Fund Medi-Cal spending, 2025–26", "$1.4 billion higher"], "b": ["why", "much of it repayments"], "arrows": false}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.35, 0.55, 0.7, 1.22, 1.55, 2.1, 2.31]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "And it isn’t over. In May 2026, the agency held back money again.", "t0": 66.07, "t1": 70.56, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Deferral CA/2026/1/E/03/MAP", "kicker": "Withheld again", "sub": "13 May 2026: drug rebates not passed back"}, "emph": ["again"], "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.32, 0.56, 1.49, 1.7, 1.88, 2.14, 2.85, 3.02, 3.46, 3.68, 3.91, 4.14]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "Drug rebates for this group, not returned to Washington.", "t0": 70.68, "t1": 73.25, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Deferral CA/2026/1/E/03/MAP", "kicker": "Withheld again", "sub": "13 May 2026: drug rebates not passed back"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.63, 0.75, 0.91, 1.38, 1.58, 1.92, 2.01]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "suspicious[2].why"], "text": "The letter calls it the 25th repeat.", "t0": 73.37, "t1": 75.19, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "25", "label": "repeats of the same deferral"}, "emph": ["25th"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.4, 0.68, 0.77, 0.87, 1.46]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what"], "text": "120,195,149 dollars, in all.", "t0": 75.31, "t1": 77.98, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$120,195,149", "label": "held back over drug rebates, in all", "sub": "back in July 2026; absent from the October letter"}, "emph": ["120,195,149"], "wt": [0.0, 0.31, 0.45, 0.68, 0.96, 1.21, 1.41, 1.69, 2.22, 2.43]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].what"], "text": "A new one, 4,638,583 dollars,", "t0": 78.6, "t1": 81.18, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "van", "label": "Claims coded as emergencies", "kicker": "A new deferral", "sub": "“solely based on” pregnancy-related codes", "chip": "$4,638,583"}, "emph": ["4,638,583"], "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.33, 0.66, 0.98, 1.19, 1.43, 1.68, 1.96]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "suspicious[3].what"], "text": "was for care claimed as emergencies, based only on pregnancy codes.", "t0": 81.18, "t1": 84.45, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "van", "label": "Claims coded as emergencies", "kicker": "A new deferral", "sub": "“solely based on” pregnancy-related codes", "chip": "$4,638,583"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.21, 0.34, 0.56, 0.88, 0.99, 1.81, 2.11, 2.34, 2.47, 2.91]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why"], "text": "Emergency care is what Washington pays for. Coding ordinary care as emergency care shifts the bill.", "t0": 84.57, "t1": 89.57, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Coding ordinary care as emergency care shifts the bill."}, "emph": ["shifts the bill"], "wt": [0.0, 0.57, 0.8, 0.89, 1.07, 1.5, 1.74, 2.44, 2.77, 3.19, 3.45, 3.57, 4.05, 4.3, 4.57, 4.68]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "sfmap", "ref": ["story[1]", "actors[5]"], "text": "In San Francisco, 23,061 residents had this coverage in July 2026.", "t0": 89.69, "t1": 94.79, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "sfmap", "pins": [{"place": "cityhall", "name": "SF Human Services Agency", "sub": "decides who qualifies"}], "zoomOn": "cityhall", "scale": 1.9, "kicker": "23,061 enrolled, July 2026"}, "emph": ["23,061"], "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.36, 1.29, 1.81, 2.21, 2.73, 3.15, 3.31, 3.49, 3.83, 3.92, 4.23, 4.49]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "suspicious[4].what"], "text": "In November 2025, the State budgeted nothing for administrative deferrals.", "t0": 95.01, "t1": 98.98, "shot": "b16b", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["State budget, November 2025", "nothing for administrative deferrals"], "b": ["the next three letters withheld", "$162.9 million · $158.2 million · $143.8 million"], "kicker": "The budget"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.54, 0.8, 1.56, 1.71, 1.99, 2.41, 2.73, 2.89, 3.46]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "suspicious[4].why"], "text": "The next three letters withheld 162.9 million,", "t0": 99.1, "t1": 102.5, "shot": "b16c", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$162.9 million", "label": "administrative claims withheld, quarter ended 2025-12-31", "sub": "then $158.2 million, then $143.8 million"}, "emph": ["162.9 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.34, 0.6, 0.88, 1.26, 1.42, 1.68, 2.23, 2.49, 2.71]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "suspicious[4].why"], "text": "158.2 million, and 143.8 million.", "t0": 102.5, "t1": 106.66, "shot": "b16cx", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$162.9 million", "label": "administrative claims withheld, quarter ended 2025-12-31", "sub": "then $158.2 million, then $143.8 million"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.26, 0.52, 1.0, 1.23, 1.43, 2.16, 2.4, 2.56, 2.81, 3.37, 3.61, 3.8]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what"], "text": "In May 2026, the State raised its figures. That comparison is this project’s.", "t0": 107.08, "t1": 111.69, "shot": "b16c", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$162.9 million", "label": "administrative claims withheld, quarter ended 2025-12-31", "sub": "then $158.2 million, then $143.8 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.35, 0.61, 1.34, 1.51, 1.84, 2.09, 2.23, 3.11, 3.32, 3.84, 3.94, 4.1]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[3]", "notEstablished[0]"], "text": "The records don’t show that San Francisco did anything wrong.", "t0": 111.91, "t1": 114.57, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That San Francisco or any county did anything wrong", "That the over-claiming was deliberate", "That anyone enrolled who did not qualify"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.49, 0.72, 0.95, 1.11, 1.3, 1.82, 2.0, 2.33]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[3]", "notEstablished[0]"], "text": "The claiming is the State’s. Or that it was deliberate.", "t0": 114.69, "t1": 117.07, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That San Francisco or any county did anything wrong", "That the over-claiming was deliberate", "That anyone enrolled who did not qualify"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.5, 0.61, 0.71, 1.4, 1.63, 1.76, 1.85, 1.96]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[1]"], "text": "What would settle it? The State’s replies to each deferral, and the percentage it uses today.", "t0": 117.19, "t1": 121.89, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The State’s replies to each deferral, and repayments by year"}, {"who": "", "what": "The percentage used today to split plan payments"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.31, 0.59, 1.16, 1.31, 1.62, 2.01, 2.15, 2.36, 2.96, 3.19, 3.29, 3.78, 3.91, 4.25]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "The audit findings are closed. The agency withheld money again in May, July and October 2026.", "t0": 122.01, "t1": 127.26, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.39, 0.78, 0.88, 1.58, 1.74, 2.13, 2.51, 2.77, 3.08, 3.21, 3.49, 3.86, 3.99, 4.42, 4.68]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 127.38, "t1": 129.27, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.57, 0.71, 0.92, 0.99, 1.09, 1.32, 1.57]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The finding", "lead1": "An old formula", "lead2": "More than $500 million", "lead3": "The 25th repeat", "lead4": "Coded as emergencies", "lead5": "The budget bet", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "dossier", "hook": "contrast"}